        "-      <div>Steps above $2/L$ lose the convergence guarantee and can diverge (every such step does on $\\tfrac L2x^2$), persistent gradient noise generally stops constant-step SGD from converging exactly, a zero gradient can be a saddle, and rates hide constants. Bisection on a certified radius finds the largest radius <em>this verifier</em> certifies: with an incomplete verifier, \"not certified\" is not a counterexample.</div>",
