        "-    <p>and total probability gives marginals, $\\mathbb P(s_1=s')=\\sum_{s,a}\\mu(s)\\,\\pi(a\\mid s)\\,P(s'\\mid s,a)$. For instance, from $\\mu=\\delta_{s_0}$ with two actions of probability $0.5$ each that reach an unsafe state with probabilities $0.2$ and $0.6$, $\\mathbb P(s_1\\text{ unsafe})=0.5\\cdot0.2+0.5\\cdot0.6=0.4$. Decorations such as $\\mathbb P^\\pi_\\mu$ or $\\mathbb E_{\\tau\\sim\\pi}$ record which $\\mu$, $\\pi$ and $P$ generate the trajectory; change any of them and every probability changes.</p>",
