        "+        <em>Setting.</em> A convex program with $d$ decision variables and uncertain convex constraints $\\theta\\in\\Theta_\\delta$, $\\delta\\sim P$ (in this box $\\delta$ is the uncertain parameter, as in the scenario literature, not a failure probability; $\\theta$ is the decision variable, not a policy parameter). Solve the <em>scenario program</em> $\\min c^\\top\\theta$ s.t. $\\theta\\in\\Theta_{\\delta^{(i)}}$ for $N$ i.i.d. samples; the required finite instances, including singleton problems, constraint removals and one-constraint augmentations, are assumed feasible with nonempty feasible interiors and attained unique minimisers of the original linear objective; the optimiser and violation event are measurable. Merely selecting one point from a nonunique optimum set does not supply these assumptions: a tie-break variant needs its own support/compression argument before using the same dimension-$d$ bound. Violation probability: $V(\\theta)=P\\{\\delta:\\theta\\notin\\Theta_\\delta\\}$.<br>",
