        "             <p><strong>(e)</strong> <span class=\"math-scroll\">$|K_0|+|K_1|=|\\sin\\theta|\\sqrt{\\rho^2-P}+|\\cos\\theta|\\sqrt P\\le\\sqrt{\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta}\\,\\sqrt{\\rho^2-P+P}=\\rho$</span> by Cauchy&ndash;Schwarz: the parameterization cannot violate the bound. Equality iff $\\tan^2\\theta=(\\rho^2-P)/P$; for $P=\\rho^2/2$ (here) that is $\\theta=\\pi/4$, giving $K_0=K_1=0.5$ and gain exactly 1.</p>",
